  "title": "BigP3BCI Study B — 6x6 checkerboard, multi-session (19 healthy subjects)",
  "description": "BigP3BCI Study B is a derivative EEG dataset containing P300 brain-computer interface recordings from 19 patients with ALS across 8 sessions each, using a 6x6 checkerboard visual speller paradigm. The dataset comprises 16-channel EEG data sampled at 256 Hz, annotated with target and non-target event labels using HED 8.4.0 schema. Study B is derived from the larger BigP3BCI initiative hosted on PhysioNet.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired using a g.USBamp amplifier (g.tec) with 16 channels in standard 10-20 montage at 256 Hz sampling rate. The experimental paradigm employed a 6x6 checkerboard visual speller with target and non-target stimulus presentations. Data were processed using the MOABB (Mother of All BCI Benchmarks) framework version 1.5.0 for P300 ERP feature extraction. Cross-validation employed a calibration-then-test method with within-subject evaluation.",
